1
00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:03,380
Andrew, ik weet dat je veel vibe-coding doet.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,087
Hoe voel je je ervan hoe het heeft veranderd?

3
00:00:06,107 --> 00:00:13,888
En vooral nu, in sommige manieren zie ik een gevoel van, we kunnen beginnen met ideeën, in plaats van necessair code of technische specifiek.

4
00:00:14,645 --> 00:00:30,915
Dank u wel.

5
00:00:30,895 --> 00:00:33,982
Coding of AI, I'm mentally exhausted.

6
00:00:34,002 --> 00:00:35,866
So I have very mixed feelings about that term.

7
00:00:35,886 --> 00:00:38,651
I tend to call it AI coding these days.

8
00:00:38,712 --> 00:00:44,584
And maybe, I actually have a, you know, listening to, a lot of my teams use lovable v0 and so on.

9
00:00:44,564 --> 00:00:55,160
There's actually one interesting thing I've seen, which is among people entering software coding for the first time, I see a little bit of sometimes insecurity, maybe imposter syndrome.

10
00:00:55,221 --> 00:00:57,083
I actually have a request to make of all of you.

11
00:00:57,104 --> 00:01:00,649
So this lesson I learned in the early days of machine learning, which is...

12
00:01:00,629 --> 00:01:09,213
Not a single time did I ever see any senior machine learning person go to a junior person and say the work you did is not actually machine learning.

13
00:01:09,233 --> 00:01:11,820
I have seen that like zero times in my career.

14
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:20,523
So what I saw, one of the reasons I think machine learning AI won, why it took off, was because if you want to call yourself a machine learning person, good enough for me, you're one of us.

15
00:01:20,544 --> 00:01:25,557
And what I hope we can do is, when we see someone that's not an official developer...

16
00:01:25,537 --> 00:01:30,936
Als ze hun code schrijven, als ze zich de ontwikkelaar willen noemen, dan is dat goed genoeg voor mij.

17
00:01:30,956 --> 00:01:31,639
Ze zijn een van ons.

18
00:01:31,659 --> 00:01:34,649
En ik vind dat het is dat echt aanwezige, welkomende gemeenschap.

19
00:01:34,669 --> 00:01:36,897
We gaan naar al die mensen die, weet je...

20
00:01:36,877 --> 00:01:39,582
did not have a CS degree or whatever.

21
00:01:39,683 --> 00:01:43,290
And I actually routinely go to my team and they did something lovable.

22
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:46,516
I routinely go and say, congrats, you're now one of us.

23
00:01:46,536 --> 00:01:51,105
And I hope we can keep doing that and just embrace everyone to get everyone to code.

24
00:01:51,592 --> 00:01:59,998
Maybe also to add to both of what you said is that one of the big differences of the current generation tools that are based on AI versus the last generation of...



